<h2 class="mb-4">Unpoly Demo</h2>

<p>
  This application demonstrates how <a href="https://unpoly.com">Unpoly</a> enhances server-rendered HTML
  to feel like a single-page app (SPA).
</p>

<p class="d-block d-md-none alert alert-danger">
  View this demo on a PC or tablet.
</p>

<p>
  The demo is divided into four unconnected mini-apps:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>
    <%= link_to 'Notes', notes_path, 'up-follow': true %>
    shows how links and forms can <a href="https://unpoly.com/targeting-fragments">update fragments</a> (instead of swapping the whole page).
  </li>
  <li>
    <%= link_to 'Companies', companies_path, 'up-follow': true %> and <%= link_to 'projects', projects_path %>
    shows how boring CRUD screens can be enhanced using <a href="https://unpoly.com/targeting-fragments">opening overlays</a> and <a href="https://unpoly.com/subinteractions">subinteractions</a>.
  </li>
  <li>
    <%= link_to 'Tasks', tasks_path, 'up-follow': true %> demonstrates <a href="https://unpoly.com/optimistic-rendering">optimistic rendering</a>.
  </li>
  <li>
    <%= link_to 'Shipping', new_shipping_path, 'up-follow': true %> shows a <a href="https://unpoly.com/reactive-server-forms">reactive form</a> with many dependent fields.
  </li>
</ul>

<p>
  <b>All data is scoped to your session</b>, so feel free to change or delete everything.
</p>

<p>
  Clicking a <b>green dot</b>
  <%= tour_dot do %>
    <p><b>This is a hint!</b></p>
    <p>Watch out for more green dots throughout the demo app.</p>
  <% end %>&nbsp;
  will reveal a hint about what you can discover here.
</p>

<p>
  Using the <b>bottom bar</b> you can modify your browsing experience.
  E.g. you can intentially slow down the server in order to better observer loading state.

</p>

<h4 class="mt-4 mb-3">Source code</h4>

<p>
  Unpoly apps are mostly just HTML. Use your browser's DevTools to look at links, forms and their <code>up-</code>prefixed attributes.
</p>

<p>
  The server code can be cloned from the <a href="https://github.com/unpoly/unpoly-demo">unpoly-demo</a> repository:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>
    The <b>backend</b> is written in Ruby, but you can use Unpoly with any backend that renders HTML on the server.
  </li>

  <li>
    The <b>frontend</b> contains <a href="https://github.com/unpoly/unpoly-demo/blob/master/app/assets/javascripts">no significant JavaScript</a>
    aside from Unpoly itself. The CSS is <a href="https://github.com/unpoly/unpoly-demo/blob/master/app/assets/stylesheets">just Bootstrap 4</a>
    with minimal tweaks.
  </li>

</ul>

